      "worked": "Let $f(x)=4e^{x}-2x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x) &= 4e^{x}-2\\\\f'(0) &= 4e^{0}-2=2\\\\f(0) &= 4e^{0}-2(0)=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so $m_N=-\\dfrac{1}{2}$. Using the point $(0,4)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-4 &= -\\frac{1}{2}(x-0)\\\\y &= -\\frac{1}{2}x+4\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
